<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">mutations</ansi>

The Chrysalis does not merely sicken — over time it rewrites those it touches.
As you live and fight and work, your body drifts toward the shape your deeds
suggest, and the Chrysalis makes that shape flesh. What you become is not chosen
from a menu; it grows from how you play.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ The Ring of Change ━━━</ansi>

Mutations are arranged as a great ring of nine <ansi fg="white-bold">clusters</ansi>, each a distinct way
of being:

  <ansi fg="yellow">Colossus</ansi>   size and smashing might      <ansi fg="yellow">Ravener</ansi>    feral, unarmed ferocity
  <ansi fg="yellow">Ironhide</ansi>   the hide that fights back     <ansi fg="yellow">Stalker</ansi>    stealth and venom
  <ansi fg="yellow">Ethereal</ansi>   incorporeal, psychic power    <ansi fg="yellow">Manifester</ansi> brood and summoning
  <ansi fg="yellow">Zealot</ansi>     voice, presence, command      <ansi fg="yellow">Weaver</ansi>     control, web, disruption
  <ansi fg="yellow">Trickster</ansi>  illusion and quicksilver guile

Clusters lean to one of two <ansi fg="white-bold">poles</ansi> — the <ansi fg="magenta">Body</ansi> (raw flesh) or <ansi fg="magenta">Belief</ansi> (will
made real). A few are hybrids, shallow on both. Commit deeply to one pole and the
opposite begins to bite.

At the heart of the ring is the <ansi fg="white-bold">Center</ansi> — the generalist path everyone begins
on: light, adaptable enablers open to anyone, and the road to flight for those who
stay unspecialised.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ How You Drift ━━━</ansi>

You cannot pick a mutation. Instead, the skills you <ansi fg="white-bold">use</ansi> pull you toward the
clusters they suit — swing a sword and you drift toward Colossus; strike unarmed
toward Ravener; sneak or shoot toward Stalker; cast toward Ethereal; sway others
toward Zealot; call forth companions toward Manifester; ply a craft toward the
maker's path. As your affinity for a cluster grows, its mutations come within reach,
and combat is what pushes a new one to finally emerge.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Depth, Keystones, and Apexes ━━━</ansi>

Each cluster runs from shallow <ansi fg="white-bold">keystones</ansi> to a single towering <ansi fg="white-bold">apex</ansi> — an
always-on transformation (Living Carapace, Colossus Form, Discorporation, and their
kin). An apex is earned, not given: you must first grow the keystones along its
spine. Deeper mutations are rarer and demand real, sustained commitment to their
cluster before they will take.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Bridges and the Maker's Path ━━━</ansi>

Where two clusters meet, a <ansi fg="white-bold">bridge</ansi> mutation belongs to both, stitching the ring
together and reachable from either side. And crafters have their own home — the
<ansi fg="white-bold">Chrysifier</ansi>, the maker's cluster within the Center, grown by working the crafts
rather than fighting.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Trade-offs and Conflicts ━━━</ansi>

The Chrysalis never improves you cleanly — most changes trade one capability for
another, and some mutations flatly conflict and cannot share a body. Some species
also carry <ansi fg="white-bold">intrinsic</ansi> mutations, natural gifts of their kind; machines and the
like are untouched by the Chrysalis entirely.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Commands ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">mutations</ansi>           List your current mutations and what they do.
  <ansi fg="command">status</ansi>              Shows your mutations in your stat panel.

